adv_07_cli_and_mcp {
    Audience: developers wiring CI, scripts, or agent tooling who need the same graph operations outside the editor.
    Outcome: run `reqlan search`, `analyse`, and `parse` headlessly; understand shared `.reqlan` index and one-base-per-run discipline; install Cursor skills / MCP; compare CLI output to chat search.
    Runtime: 10–12 min.
    Demo: advanced baseline in integrated terminal at repo root; `.reqlan` indexed; Cursor host preferred for skills beat — VS Code fallback with palette mention only.
    Related: [cli_package] [commands] [mcp_tools] [cursor_skills_install] [chat_skill_naming] [ai_integration] [base] [multi_base_environment]
    @example {
        ```bash
        # From reqlan-tutorials-demo/ (active base at root)
        npx reqlan search "empty password"
        npx reqlan analyse --idea login_api
        npx reqlan parse reqs/auth.rq
        npx reqlan parse reqs/ --fail-on-diagnostics
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Terminal at demo workspace root. Prompt shows `reqlan-tutorials-demo`. Run `npx reqlan search "empty password"`.

        VO: The CLI speaks to the same analytical API as the extension and MCP tools.
            Headless CI, local scripts, and editors share one index under the active base's `.reqlan`.

        SCR: Show compact search results — idea name, path, short snippet. Then `npx reqlan analyse --idea login_api`.

        VO: Analyse expands one idea the way a careful human would — references, files, attributes —
            without dumping the whole graph as JSON unless you ask for it.

        SCR: `npx reqlan parse reqs/auth.rq` — clean output. Optional: `parse reqs/ --fail-on-diagnostics` mentioned as CI pattern.

        VO: Parse is your gate in CI. Fail the build when requirements stop parsing — same sources the extension indexes.

        SCR: Explorer: `.reqlan/` visible. Do not open sqlite. Active base picker flash — "one selected base per CLI run".

        VO: Treat the index as tooling memory, not something you hand-edit.
            CLI and MCP select one base at a time — nested bases are separate runs, same craft as context and export.

        SCR: Command Palette: `Reqlan: Install Cursor Skills` (Cursor host) or show `.cursor/skills` tree at high level. MCP config mention — no deep edit on camera.

        VO: Skills give agents the `rq-` prefix commands humans use in chat —
            search, file context, build requirement — with the same token discipline.

        SCR: Chat: `/rq-search empty password` or `@reqlan /rq-search`. Same hit as CLI. Side-by-side or cut between terminal and chat.

        VO: If CLI and chat disagree, the active base or cwd is usually wrong — not two different graphs.

        SCR: Misconception beat — running CLI from a parent monorepo folder without `--cwd` (slide fix: `npx reqlan --cwd reqlan-tutorials-demo search …`).

        VO: Try this: wire a CI step that runs `reqlan parse` on `reqs/` and fails the build on diagnostics.

        SCR: End card → "Patterns that age well".
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 07
            heading CLI and MCP
            body Same graph API — terminal, CI, agents, and the editor.
            asset logo
            notes The CLI speaks to the same analytical API as the extension and MCP tools.
        }
        {
            id search
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Headless search
            body Concise output. Same index under .reqlan.
            code_lang bash
            code npx reqlan search "empty password"
            notes Compact results on purpose — same discipline as chat search.
        }
        {
            id analyse-parse
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Analyse and parse
            body One idea expanded. Parse as CI gate on reqs/.
            code_lang bash
            code npx reqlan analyse --idea login_api / parse reqs/ --fail-on-diagnostics
            notes Fail the build when requirements stop parsing.
        }
        {
            id index-base
            transition none
            background brand-contrast
            heading One base per run
            body Index is tooling memory. Nested bases = separate runs.
            code_lang txt
            code demo/.reqlan/ · --cwd · active base picker
            notes Do not hand-edit the index. Confirm cwd when results look wrong.
        }
        {
            id skills
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Install Cursor skills
            body rq- prefix commands for agents — search, context, build.
            asset chat-search
            code Reqlan: Install Cursor Skills
            notes Skills mirror human chat commands with token discipline.
        }
        {
            id parity
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading CLI vs chat parity
            body Same query, same hit — if not, check cwd and active base.
            code_lang txt
            code npx reqlan search … / @reqlan /rq-search …
            notes Two hosts, one analytical core.
        }
        {
            id cwd-trap
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Wrong folder trap
            body Parent monorepo? Pass --cwd to the demo base.
            code_lang bash
            code npx reqlan --cwd reqlan-tutorials-demo search "empty password"
            notes CLI and chat disagree → cwd or active base is usually wrong.
        }
        {
            id try-this
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            heading Try this
            body Wire CI to run reqlan parse on reqs/ and fail on diagnostics.
            fragments Next — Modelling patterns
            notes Headless CI, local scripts, and editors share one index.
        }
    )
}

adv_08_modelling_patterns {
    Audience: viewers finishing the advanced series who want durable habits for graphs that stay readable as they grow — in software or elsewhere.
    Outcome: apply five modelling habits (thin ideas, links over duplication, active-base discipline, purposeful attributes, chosen maps); recognize the same language in a non-software vignette; leave with a recap mantra tied to [mission_statement].
    Runtime: 10–11 min.
    Demo: advanced baseline complete; create `reqs/newsletter.rq` live or open pre-staged file; `media/interviews/` folder exists; product/auth graph unchanged in background.
    Related: [simplicity] [general_purpose] [cartographic_map] [mission_statement] [llm_first] [base] [phonebook]
    @example {
        ```rq
        // Vignette — editorial / ops, still .rq
        // reqs/newsletter.rq
        issue_brief {
            June issue theme: "small tools with sharp edges".
            Lead piece must cite [interview_lee].
            @status draft
            @tags (
                editorial
            )
        }

        interview_lee {
            Interview with Lee about maintaining a tiny CLI used in production.
            Assets live under ["./media/interviews/"]
        }

        production_checklist {
            Before send: spellcheck, link check, unsubscribe footer, [issue_brief] theme echoed in subject line.
        }
        ```
    }
    @script {
        SCR: Title: "Advanced · 08 · Patterns that age well". Five-second montage: imports, graph filter, rq: comment, export browser, terminal search.

        VO: Advanced reqlan is not more syntax — it is better judgement about what deserves a name,
            what deserves a link, and what deserves to stay out of the prompt.

        SCR: New file `reqs/newsletter.rq`. Type `issue_brief` block from example — or open pre-staged file. Link to `interview_lee`. Add `@status draft`.

        VO: The language is general-purpose. Software is the common case, not the only case.
            An editorial brief is still a named idea with neighbours — same brackets, same attributes, same index.

        SCR: Add `interview_lee` with folder ref to `media/interviews/`. Add `production_checklist` linking back to `[issue_brief]`. Navigate links both ways.

        VO: Judgement beat: resist duplicating the June theme prose in three places.
            Link to `issue_brief` from the checklist — readers and models follow one source of truth.

        SCR: Ideas Summary graph on `issue_brief` — two-hop max, quick screenshot, close. Contrast with product/auth graph in editor tab switch.

        VO: Two domains, one base, one index — that is fine for a demo workspace.
            In production you might split bases when graphs serve different audiences — boundary craft, not folder hygiene for its own sake.

        SCR: Whiteboard slide — five durable habits reveal one at a time:
            1. One idea, one job
            2. Links over duplication
            3. One active base — know your graph boundary
            4. Attributes that drive a view
            5. Maps you choose, never mandatory full dumps

        VO: One idea, one job — if the name needs "and", consider splitting.
            Links over duplication — prose repeats are a smell; brackets are cheap.
            One active base — exports, CLI, and context all respect the boundary you already learned.
            Attributes that drive a view — status, tags, plans; delete the rest.
            Maps you choose — activity bar while editing, Ideas Summary when explaining.

        SCR: Return to `login_api` briefly — show slim idea with refs, not a megablock. Misconception: "document everything in one idea".

        VO: Those habits keep you aligned with why the project exists —
            semantic requirements as code for people working with LLMs, with ergonomic definition and consumption.

        SCR: End card: link pack from [phonebook] — site, docs, marketplace, GitHub. On-screen: "Write the idea. Link the neighbour. Ship the slice."

        VO: Thanks for watching the advanced series. Write the idea. Link the neighbour. Ship the slice.
    }
    @slides (
        {
            id title
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            kicker Advanced · 08
            heading Patterns that age well
            body Not more syntax — better judgement about names, links, and prompt size.
            asset logo
            notes Advanced reqlan is not more syntax — it is better judgement.
        }
        {
            id recap-montage
            transition slide
            background brand-panel
            heading Series recap
            body Imports · attributes · maps · context · comments · export · CLI · patterns
            asset montage-ide
            notes Eight themes converge on readable graphs for people and models.
        }
        {
            id vignette
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Same language, other domain
            body Editorial briefs and ops checklists are still named ideas with neighbours.
            code_lang rq
            code issue_brief { June theme… cite [interview_lee]. @status draft }
            notes Software is the common case, not the only case.
        }
        {
            id links-not-dupe
            transition fade
            background brand-contrast
            heading Links over duplication
            body production_checklist echoes [issue_brief] — does not restate the theme prose.
            code_lang rq
            code [issue_brief] theme echoed in subject line
            notes One source of truth. Brackets are cheap; repeated prose is a smell.
        }
        {
            id two-domains-one-base
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Two domains, one base
            body Demo workspace mixes product and newsletter. Production may split bases by audience.
            code_lang txt
            code product.rq + newsletter.rq · demo/.reqlan/
            notes Boundary craft when graphs serve different audiences — not folder hygiene alone.
        }
        {
            id five-habits
            transition fade
            background brand-panel
            heading Five durable habits
            body Keep the graph readable for people and models alike.
            code_lang txt
            code 1. One idea, one job / 2. Links over duplication / 3. One active base / 4. Attributes that drive a view / 5. Maps you choose
            notes Semantic requirements as code — ergonomic definition and consumption.
        }
        {
            id slim-software
            transition none
            background brand-panel
            heading Slim beats megablocks
            body login_api: prose, refs, purposeful attributes — not document everything here.
            code_lang rq
            code login_api { POST /login… [password_rules] @status in-progress }
            notes If the name needs and, consider splitting the idea.
        }
        {
            id end
            transition fade
            background brand-dark
            heading Write the idea
            body Link the neighbour. Ship the slice.
            asset logo
            fragments Back to tutorials · site · docs · marketplace
            notes Thanks for watching the advanced series.
        }
    )
}

// --- Production notes ---------------------------------------------------------

tutorial_production {
    Recording order: get-started 01→07, concepts 01→02, then advanced overview → 01→08; pickups allowed out of order.
    Before each take: reset `reqlan-tutorials-demo` to the Demo pre-state listed on the episode; confirm hop depth / filters are at defaults.
    Slide decks for [slide_decks] live under ["../../presentations/"] as authored JSONC plus generated runtime JSON and a shared player shell.
    After editing `@slides`, rewrite the matching `presentations/decks/<id>.jsonc`, update catalog blurbs in ["../../presentations/manifest.jsonc"],
    then run site `sync:presentations` so [site_reqs.sync_presentations] refreshes runtime JSON under `public/presentations/`.
    Site embeds those decks under `/tutorials` per [site_reqs.tutorials_section].
    Each episode may also ship: master video, short vertical teaser (optional), example files under a public examples/tutorials/ tree (path TBD with docs), and a transcript derived from `@script`.
    Thumbnails: dark rust / aqua; episode index; avoid clutter per [show_dont_tell].
    Accessibility: burned-in or downloadable captions from the caption-ready `@script`; avoid conveying unique info by colour alone on graph filters.
    Keep demos on extension behaviours marked `@status done` in the requirement graph; if a referenced feature is incomplete, note it on-screen as preview or skip that beat and leave `@todo` on the episode.
    @status draft
}

tutorial_success_metrics {
    Qualitative: a viewer can complete the get-started try-this prompts without reading the monorepo.
    Quantitative (once published): marketplace / site CTR from end cards; completion rate on get-started 01–03; example-repo clones or gist hits.
    Feedback loop: file issues against this `.rq` file when scripts drift from product behaviour.
}
